      "coverage": "Convex light-curve reconstruction with approximate thermal size: 83.23 km effective diameter (catalog ±1.04 km; additional shape and thermal-model uncertainty). Thermal size is used as a volume-scale approximation. An alternative pole remains possible. The grid marks unavailable imagery; rotational phase is illustrative. The physical size is approximately calibrated by assigning the AKARI thermal effective diameter to the mesh volume-equivalent diameter. Neither source mesh nor spin is modified. Convex inversion supplies only broad outline; no resolved craters, concavities, reflectance or regolith texture can be inferred. Hanuš2016 Table2 reports 29 dense light curves across three apparitions plus 516 sparse measurements. Both poles remain; the first archived solution is selected as a reproducible representative, not a proven unique orientation.",
